{
  "$comment": "Spells (D&D 5e SRD), cast from the quick bar: each of its keys (Q R T 1-5 X C, Shift for the second row) casts its square, right click the one last picked. There are no spell slots: each spell has a recovery (seconds) before it can be cast again, and a short rest recovers them all. level: the spell's own level (0: cantrip), which sets how long it takes to recover: about 0.75-2 s for a cantrip, 4-10 s for level 1, longer for each level after. Which hero learns a spell, and at what hero level, is in the class's progression (src/data/classes.json). kind: bolt (a projectile; a spell attack, d20 + proficiency + casting ability, against AC), missiles (count darts that always hit), burst (everyone within radius px of the point aimed at, within range px of the caster, or of the caster when range is 0, rolls a save against the spell DC: full damage on a failure, half on a success; area: sphere (the default: within radius px of that point), cube (a square of radius px each way from it) cone (from the caster towards the aim, range + radius px long and as wide at its end as it is long) or line (from the caster towards the aim, range px long and radius px each side of it, src/rules/SpellArea.ts); a thunder or lightning burst charges the water it reaches, and the water conducts it to everyone standing in it), heal (the caster, dice + casting ability; with a radius, every hero within it). damage: dice notation; damageType: fire, cold, lightning, force, necrotic, radiant, thunder, acid, psychic. effect: [shape, colour] from src/assets/Effects.ts, played where it strikes (and as its icon); effectScale sizes it. buff: lasts on the caster (buff: blade_ward or stoneskin resist weapons' damage, shield +5 AC, mage_armor AC 13 + DEX until a long rest, false_life temporary hit points of its dice; seconds: how long, 0 until a long rest). zone: stays where it is cast (on the caster when range is 0, following them) for seconds, striking everyone in its radius at once and every 6 seconds after (a save for half when it has one). water: a puddle of radius px where aimed (a thunder or lightning spell charges it, a lightning bolt flying over it too). concentration: held by concentration, one spell at a time; damage may break it (a Constitution save). drain: the share of a bolt's damage its caster heals. true_strike (a buff, held by concentration): the caster's next attack roll has advantage. lights (Dancing Lights): four lights within range (round the caster when aimed at them) for seconds, shedding light; foes within radius px of them save (WIS) or are drawn to them. surface (Grease): grease of radius px where aimed for seconds: difficult terrain, a save (DEX) or fall prone, set alight by fire. sleep (Sleep): a mote that flies as a bolt does and settles on the first creature it touches: damage is the hit points it lulls (5d8, 2d8 more a level above the 1st); one with no more falls asleep for seconds, until hurt (undead are not affected). ally (Longstrider, Protection from Evil and Good): a buff on the hero nearest the point aimed at, within range px (the caster when none is near it): longstrider +10 feet of speed, protection_from_evil_and_good: undead attack them at disadvantage. fog (Fog Cloud): a cloud of radius px where aimed for seconds: whoever is in it is heavily obscured (attacks into it, out of it and within it at disadvantage; enemies cannot see heroes in or behind it); dark: true makes it Darkness (darker still, and light does not shine in it). hex (Charm Person, Tasha's Hideous Laughter, Blindness/Deafness, Hold Person, Crown of Madness): the foe under the crosshair within range px saves (save) or is held in its condition (charmed, laughing, blinded or deafened as bound, paralyzed, maddened) for seconds, saving again every 6 seconds (systems/SpellHolds.ts); creatures: the creature types it takes; minIntelligence: the least Intelligence it takes; targetsPerLevel: the foes more it takes for each level it is cast above its own (Charm Person, Blindness, Hold Person: one). A bolt with a condition (Ray of Enfeeblement) lays it on a hit instead of damage (enfeebled: half damage with Strength weapons). buff blur (attacks at disadvantage), mirror_image (count duplicates), shadow_blade (the weapon in hand becomes a blade of damage dice and type), see_invisibility (invisible creatures within radius px are seen, and save or are revealed); ally magic_weapon (+1 to hit and damage, +2 cast at 4th, +3 at 6th), invisibility (unseen until it attacks or casts). zone with rolls (Flaming Sphere): it rolls towards where its caster aims, 30 feet a round. gust (Gust of Wind): a line from the caster towards the aim, held while it lasts: whoever is in it saves (save) once a round or is pushed push feet along it (into a pit, if one lies that way), and it scatters fog. teleport (Misty Step): the caster steps through mist to a free place it can see within range px. surface with surface: web (Web): webs in a cube of radius px each way: difficult terrain, a save (DEX) or restrained, burnt away by fire.",
